WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.716 --> 00:00:06.686
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:19.432
[sputtering]

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:22.168
I-I can't sleep.  I know I saw a bat.

00:00:22.168 --> 00:00:25.538
It's just waiting until
I'm asleep to bite my face off.

00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:26.272
Where is it?

00:00:27.007 --> 00:00:29.275
Look at that ceiling, it could be anywhere.

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:32.178
This is a losing battle;
I'm getting out of here.

00:00:32.178 --> 00:00:35.281
The feng shui of this room sucks anyway.

00:00:35.281 --> 00:00:37.450
Why does this room even exist?

00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:38.551
It doesn't.

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:41.187
I'm leaving it, therefore
it ceases to exist.

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:45.859
Well, not really, but that's
how my memory needs to file it.

00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:48.294
Why are there enormous pistons here?

00:00:48.294 --> 00:00:51.197
If there was something on the belt,
it would just crush it to the side

00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:52.766
and not send it anywhere.

00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:54.034
So, why would...

00:00:55.201 --> 00:00:56.569
Yes, master.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.472
Wait, no!  Stop!

00:00:59.506 --> 00:01:02.642
I really don't understand
what the purpose of this is.

00:01:02.642 --> 00:01:04.277
Other than to scare me.

00:01:04.277 --> 00:01:10.083
But, there are cheaper and more
energy-efficient ways of doing that.

00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:13.219
I would feel better about
this experience if I knew that

00:01:13.253 --> 00:01:17.490
on the other side of these walls,
a giant robot was moving its fingers.

00:01:18.558 --> 00:01:20.693
It would seem more noble then.

00:01:20.693 --> 00:01:22.062
Oh wow.  Seriously?

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:24.431
We actually have crushers of death, too?

00:01:24.431 --> 00:01:26.099
What are we making in this factory?

00:01:26.099 --> 00:01:27.801
Something flat.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.502
Jesus Christ...

00:01:29.536 --> 00:01:30.637
Oh-kyaaah!

00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:32.972
Oh, they have
different stomping patterns!

00:01:32.972 --> 00:01:34.808
Yeah, that's really necessary!

00:01:34.808 --> 00:01:36.309
Yaaah!

00:01:36.309 --> 00:01:37.710
Oh, this one's full of tricks!

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.979
It's tapping out Morse
on the fucking belt!

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:41.448
Red lights, walking backwards,

00:01:41.481 --> 00:01:43.983
GIVE ME SOME MORE PRESSURE!
I DON'T HAVE ENOUGH!

00:01:43.983 --> 00:01:47.087
YES!  BIOHAZARD!
PERFECT!  THANK YOU!

00:01:47.087 --> 00:01:49.222
YAAAH!  FALLING TO MY DEATH!

00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:51.458
TANK OF ACID!  SUPERB!

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:52.592
Sidestepping...

00:01:53.793 --> 00:01:57.931
I hear fire... but I don't see fire.

00:01:57.931 --> 00:02:00.100
It must be space fire.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.736
But I am not a space man, thus,
I do not need to be extinguished.

00:02:04.204 --> 00:02:06.039
Man, look at these landings.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:08.842
Sideways freefalling
on moving conveyor belts.

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.643
I am a cat!

00:02:10.677 --> 00:02:13.480
It's kind of pissing me off
this whole place is abandoned.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.949
I don't have anyone to show off to.

00:02:15.949 --> 00:02:17.851
If the workers were here, they could say,

00:02:17.884 --> 00:02:22.555
"Hey, look at him! He's ridin' a conveyor
belt! I've always wanted to do that!"

00:02:22.555 --> 00:02:25.492
Whoa, oh my God. I can
feel the heat from here.

00:02:25.492 --> 00:02:26.659
I need to get off here.

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:27.994
Maybe this way...

00:02:27.994 --> 00:02:28.962
No, this way sucks.

00:02:28.962 --> 00:02:30.230
Okay, yeah, this'll work.

00:02:30.997 --> 00:02:32.765
Okay, that's the end of the ride.

00:02:32.765 --> 00:02:36.169
I can dodge giant crushers;
I can't dodge an incinerator.

00:02:36.169 --> 00:02:38.671
I would need much better reflexes.

00:02:40.373 --> 00:02:42.142
And a more nebulous body.

00:02:42.142 --> 00:02:45.111
Until you can rearrange atomic
particles the way you want them,

00:02:45.111 --> 00:02:48.414
I don't think anyone can
ever claim to have true power.

00:02:48.448 --> 00:02:50.416
Oh, what's this?  Another dead end?

00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:51.417
Okay...

00:02:52.585 --> 00:02:57.023
Hey, then why have safety railing and a
walkway if no one can get up here anyway?

00:02:57.023 --> 00:03:01.427
I cheated!  I came in on the conveyor
belt!  No one's supposed to do that!

00:03:02.529 --> 00:03:04.531
I could expect this crap on Mars.

00:03:04.531 --> 00:03:06.933
They have a 1/3 gravity;
I could just hop up here.

00:03:06.933 --> 00:03:08.334
Not on Earth!

00:03:09.536 --> 00:03:11.404
Well, that drop wasn't too bad.

00:03:11.404 --> 00:03:13.339
Maybe I'm developing a resistance.

00:03:13.339 --> 00:03:17.177
It's like that joke on the Addams Family
where Gomez tells an insurance agent

00:03:17.177 --> 00:03:20.180
he's learning to skydive with a
smaller and smaller parachute

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.915
until he doesn't need one at all.

00:03:21.915 --> 00:03:23.249
That was a cool show.

00:03:23.249 --> 00:03:25.051
I identified with Thing.

00:03:25.051 --> 00:03:26.619
What is this thing?

00:03:26.619 --> 00:03:28.354
It looks like a shrine.

00:03:28.354 --> 00:03:31.724
Maybe it breaks so much, they decided to
install a light here for the workers

00:03:31.758 --> 00:03:33.459
rather than replace it.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:37.597
If your logic acts under the assumption
that this thing will be breaking forever,

00:03:37.597 --> 00:03:40.200
then some decisions
start making more sense.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.103
Something tells me you're not going to
contribute anything to this conversation.

00:03:44.904 --> 00:03:46.172
I'm a good debater.

00:03:46.172 --> 00:03:49.609
Though, you do make a strong argument
for not going that way.

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:53.546
All right.  I'm agnostic about
which concrete corridor I take,

00:03:53.546 --> 00:03:57.850
having no other information than
it's another concrete corridor.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:01.921
Oh, it's a dead end...
with no storage here or anything.

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:03.389
I see.

00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:05.358
We're playing that game again.

00:04:05.358 --> 00:04:10.396
Well, I do have...criticisms...
about how this place is structured.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.400
Maybe I'm not one to talk,
because I shouldn't even be here.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.135
But, you shouldn't either.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.672
So, there's that.

00:04:19.672 --> 00:04:20.907
Oh, hey, a door.

00:04:20.907 --> 00:04:23.643
This means that the builders
of this temple were civilized.

00:04:23.643 --> 00:04:24.944
[lock jiggles]

00:04:24.944 --> 00:04:26.379
No...

00:04:26.379 --> 00:04:27.780
No, my mistake.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.048
They're savages.

00:04:29.048 --> 00:04:31.784
But, who am I to question their ways?

00:04:31.784 --> 00:04:34.887
Maybe they play hide-and-go-seek
here when it's a slow shift.

00:04:34.887 --> 00:04:38.224
Maybe...they're doing it right now!

00:04:38.224 --> 00:04:41.160
And you...are...it.

00:04:42.061 --> 00:04:43.129
I win.

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:45.265
Okay, so who's more at fault here?

00:04:45.265 --> 00:04:48.968
Me, for entering this place like I'm
trying to break into the Pentagon?

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:53.373
Or, everyone else, for not
giving me an exit to begin with?

00:04:53.373 --> 00:04:55.008
And another dead end.

00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:56.609
No!  Two dead ends.

00:04:56.609 --> 00:04:57.644
Classy.

00:04:57.677 --> 00:04:59.946
Okay, so that answers that question.

00:04:59.946 --> 00:05:02.415
It is NOT my fault,

00:05:02.415 --> 00:05:04.584
but will I be able to prove it?

00:05:04.584 --> 00:05:05.918
I mean, I looked.

00:05:05.918 --> 00:05:10.123
There was no entrance or exit
from that other factory wing.

00:05:10.123 --> 00:05:13.192
But, of course, some jackass
is going to come along later

00:05:13.192 --> 00:05:16.729
and show me an obvious one
in a place I already looked.

00:05:16.763 --> 00:05:18.131
It wasn't there earlier.

00:05:18.131 --> 00:05:20.433
Like there's going to be
one here tomorrow, I bet.

00:05:20.433 --> 00:05:24.237
Fucking gremlins are building it right
now, just so I look like an idiot later.

00:05:24.237 --> 00:05:28.074
When the truth is, I arrived
at this reality a little too early.

00:05:28.074 --> 00:05:29.375
Oh. "Stairs".

00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:30.576
That'll work.

00:05:30.576 --> 00:05:31.244
Shit.

00:05:31.911 --> 00:05:34.480
I feel like strangling something.

00:05:34.514 --> 00:05:36.849
It would be fun to be
known as a strangler.

00:05:36.883 --> 00:05:40.753
I mean, it wouldn't be worth it to
strangle people just to get the name,

00:05:40.753 --> 00:05:44.691
but if the police came up with a name
for me like "The Sneaky Strangler",

00:05:44.691 --> 00:05:45.758
that would be cool.

00:05:45.758 --> 00:05:48.594
Okay, good.  This sign points straight,

00:05:48.594 --> 00:05:50.596
not left four times in a row.

00:05:50.596 --> 00:05:52.098
That would piss me off.

00:05:52.098 --> 00:05:54.367
Oh, what am I talking about?
I have a Ph.D.

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.602
They'd call me "Dr. Stranglelove".

00:05:56.602 --> 00:06:00.273
Actually, that could be a porn name,
but only for the edgier stuff.

00:06:00.273 --> 00:06:00.773
Ah.

00:06:00.807 --> 00:06:01.274
[gun clicks]

00:06:01.274 --> 00:06:01.774
OH GOD!

00:06:01.808 --> 00:06:02.642
I'M OUT OF AMMO!

00:06:02.642 --> 00:06:04.243
WHOSE JOB WAS IT TO RELOAD?!

00:06:04.243 --> 00:06:05.244
THEY'RE FIRED!

00:06:05.244 --> 00:06:06.879
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
'THERE'S NO AMMO LEFT'?!

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:08.514
YOU'RE FIRED, TOO!

00:06:08.548 --> 00:06:11.617
I can't delegate anything around here!

00:06:12.652 --> 00:06:15.188
Well, at least I have my backup gun.

00:06:15.188 --> 00:06:18.524
Let's just hope I don't need
a backup backup gun.

00:06:18.524 --> 00:06:20.326
Most people don't need that.

00:06:20.326 --> 00:06:22.895
Most people don't even
need a backup gun.

00:06:22.895 --> 00:06:24.931
I guess it depends on
what state you live in.

00:06:24.931 --> 00:06:26.332
Where the hell is this thing?

00:06:26.332 --> 00:06:27.600
I didn't imagine it.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:27.967
Draw!

00:06:29.569 --> 00:06:31.504
Well, it was a fair fight.

00:06:31.504 --> 00:06:33.339
No one can say it wasn't.

00:06:33.339 --> 00:06:37.310
Yeah, I guess this is presumptuous
but I have to say that--

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.779
Oh, hey, there are stairs.
That sign wasn't lying.

00:06:40.346 --> 00:06:41.748
What was I thinking about?

00:06:41.748 --> 00:06:42.949
Stairs...

00:06:43.816 --> 00:06:44.884
Alien...

00:06:45.685 --> 00:06:47.487
I wanted a banana milkshake...

00:06:47.487 --> 00:06:48.454
Oh, that's right.

00:06:48.454 --> 00:06:51.023
I'm a little disappointed by these aliens.

00:06:51.023 --> 00:06:53.393
They're not displaying
much intelligence.

00:06:53.393 --> 00:06:54.460
They're naked.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.129
They're mostly just bipeds.

00:06:56.129 --> 00:06:58.965
I could come up with
much better aliens than these.

00:06:58.965 --> 00:07:01.734
Okay...uh, hah hah!

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:03.102
Joke's over.

00:07:03.102 --> 00:07:04.704
Where's the exit?

00:07:04.704 --> 00:07:06.305
Oh, my God.

00:07:06.305 --> 00:07:09.275
Alright, I already went
through this red shrine thing,

00:07:09.275 --> 00:07:11.844
so I know where this belt goes.

00:07:12.845 --> 00:07:14.580
I guess I'll just try again.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.082
Maybe I missed something.

00:07:16.082 --> 00:07:19.752
Because, y'know, exits are
supposed to be difficult to locate.

00:07:19.752 --> 00:07:23.756
Because, God help you if somebody
exited your building by accident.

00:07:23.756 --> 00:07:26.492
Then, they'd have to come back in.

00:07:26.492 --> 00:07:27.994
Oh, hey, that's it.

00:07:27.994 --> 00:07:29.662
I didn't try this belt backwards.

00:07:30.963 --> 00:07:32.398
(gasping)
Because it's the other...

00:07:32.398 --> 00:07:33.833
one I came in on...

00:07:34.734 --> 00:07:37.036
Okay...so let's talk better aliens...

00:07:38.104 --> 00:07:39.605
It depends on the gravity...

00:07:40.339 --> 00:07:41.774
and atmosphere obviously...

00:07:42.241 --> 00:07:43.443
but, if it's like ours...

00:07:44.277 --> 00:07:46.179
what you need is all
the organs in the core...

00:07:46.979 --> 00:07:48.514
with many muscular appendages...

00:07:48.848 --> 00:07:50.683
with handlike grippers on the ends...

00:07:52.051 --> 00:07:53.853
If the inner ear...was developed...

00:07:54.086 --> 00:07:56.422
this would allow for
extremely good mobility...

00:07:57.323 --> 00:07:58.991
and a natural advantage over us...

00:07:59.425 --> 00:08:00.293
for tool use...

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.461
Huh...

00:08:01.461 --> 00:08:03.663
So, it would look like
a jointed octopus

00:08:03.663 --> 00:08:06.199
rotated on an axis or two...with hands.

00:08:06.566 --> 00:08:07.366
No!

00:08:07.366 --> 00:08:08.367
Dammit, no!

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:09.502
This is unacceptable!

00:08:11.103 --> 00:08:12.872
I remember lasers are bad!

00:08:12.872 --> 00:08:14.941
Tripmine!  That's a tripmine!

00:08:14.941 --> 00:08:16.442
Why would we do that?

00:08:16.442 --> 00:08:19.712
Either everything conforms to standards
or we blow up the assembly line.

00:08:19.712 --> 00:08:20.513
Is that it?

00:08:20.513 --> 00:08:23.015
What the hell?
This is an American company.

00:08:23.015 --> 00:08:27.086
We're not supposed to have that all-or-
nothing mentality like the Japanese.

00:08:27.086 --> 00:08:27.887
I'm going to shoot it.

00:08:27.887 --> 00:08:29.789
I don't care if it blows up the conveyor.

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:30.690
It's their fault.

00:08:31.591 --> 00:08:33.593
Dammit! This is hard.

00:08:33.593 --> 00:08:36.329
I could use the scope, but it
would just kick up in my face.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.097
Ah!

00:08:38.564 --> 00:08:40.333
Yup, I blew up the conveyor.

00:08:40.333 --> 00:08:43.603
Now the district manager has to commit
hara-kiri or something, I guess.

00:08:43.603 --> 00:08:47.173
This reminds me of those old video games
from Japan that were impossible to beat

00:08:47.173 --> 00:08:49.575
and if you died, they would tell you
how many fingers to cut off

00:08:49.575 --> 00:08:50.910
to preserve your honor.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.545
Man, that barely damaged it.

00:08:52.545 --> 00:08:54.714
I guess it was a practice explosive.

00:08:54.714 --> 00:08:56.682
Are you fucking kiddi-- TWO?!

00:08:56.682 --> 00:08:57.683
(gasping)

00:08:58.651 --> 00:08:59.619
Just in case the...

00:09:00.219 --> 00:09:00.786
first one...

00:09:01.053 --> 00:09:01.821
wasn't enough?

00:09:02.321 --> 00:09:03.389
Jesus Christ...

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.825
I can't crabwalk out of here...

00:09:06.359 --> 00:09:07.860
Okay, okay, I'll just grab the side...

00:09:08.394 --> 00:09:09.595
and squeeze through...

00:09:10.096 --> 00:09:14.066
Oh my God... it sucks big wads...

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:18.137
(straining)

00:09:18.137 --> 00:09:20.940
(gasping)

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:21.507
Fuck...

00:09:23.242 --> 00:09:25.211
I don't think I'm going
to get a nap in today.

00:09:25.811 --> 00:09:27.880
There's just too much to do.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.348
Ah, door!  Door!

00:09:29.348 --> 00:09:31.083
I-I can make time for that.

00:09:31.083 --> 00:09:35.121
If you ask me whether I'd rather
open a door or try to kill myself...

00:09:36.255 --> 00:09:37.089
Actually, scratch that.

00:09:37.089 --> 00:09:38.424
Those are shitty options.

00:09:38.424 --> 00:09:39.425
I just want to leave.

00:09:39.425 --> 00:09:42.261
Oh, this is THAT door.

00:09:42.261 --> 00:09:44.397
So, leaving was never an option.

00:09:44.397 --> 00:09:48.000
And crawling in circles until you
fucking die, THERE'S AN OPTION!

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.635
I LIKE THAT OPTION!

00:09:49.635 --> 00:09:51.470
LET'S GO WITH THAT OPTION!

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.105
BLAAAAAARRRRRGH!

00:09:56.042 --> 00:09:57.810
Actually, I was just kidding.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.500
I don't like that option.

